              "Democratic activists say Shapiro isn't pushing hard enough — a constitutional amendment requires two consecutive legislative sessions",
              "His national positioning on abortion has sometimes outpaced concrete state-level legislative action",
              "The 24-week law remains fully vulnerable if PA elects a Republican governor in 2026 or later",
              "Anti-abortion advocates say Shapiro has never engaged in good-faith legislative compromise"
            ],
            source: "PA General Assembly · Pennsylvania Capital-Star · Philadelphia Inquirer · ACLU-PA · as of April 2026"
          },
          erpo: {
            title: "Gun violence & ERPO red flag law",
            heat: "Active debate",
            heat_style: "background:rgba(245,158,11,0.1); color:#92400e; border:0.5px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.25); font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; font-size:9px; padding:2px 9px; border-radius:10px;",
            who_label: "Shapiro's position",
            for_label: "ERPO supporters",
            for_text: "Extreme Risk Protection Orders let families or police temporarily remove guns from someone in crisis before they harm themselves or others. 21 states have them. PA's gun death rate is high — this is evidence-based prevention that could pass if Shapiro applied more pressure.",
            against_label: "Second Amendment side",
            against_text: "ERPOs allow courts to strip someone's firearms without due process — based on a family member's accusation before any crime. This is unconstitutional prior restraint on a constitutional right, and the Republican Senate is right to block it.",
            position: "Supports ERPO legislation. Has repeatedly called on the Republican Senate to pass it. Signed an EO in 2024 creating PA's first Office of Gun Violence Prevention and secured a $4M DOJ grant. Vetoed a Republican bill that would have blocked future gun restrictions. ERPO has not passed as of early 2026.",
            timeline: [
              ["2023–2024", "Shapiro repeatedly calls for ERPO legislation — Republican Senate refuses to bring it to a vote"],
              ["2024", "Signs EO creating PA Office of Gun Violence Prevention — first in state history"],
              ["2024", "Secures $4M DOJ gun violence prevention grant for Pennsylvania"],
              ["2025", "Vetoes Republican bill restricting future firearms regulations"],
              ["2026", "ERPO still blocked in Senate — ~2,000 Pennsylvanians die from gun violence each year"]
            ],
            critics: [
              "ERPO has stalled for three years under Shapiro's watch — critics say he isn't applying enough legislative pressure",
              "The Office of Gun Violence Prevention has a small budget relative to the scale of the problem",
              "PA's gun death rate (~16 per 100K) is above the national average — progress under Shapiro has been slow",
              "Urban-rural divide makes gun legislation nearly impossible in the current divided legislature"
            ],
            source: "PA General Assembly · Governor's Office · Everytown for Gun Safety · Pennsylvania Capital-Star · as of April 2026"
          }
        };

        function issueModal(id) {
          var d = ISSUE_DATA[id];
          if (!d) return;
          document.getElementById('issue-modal-title').textContent = d.title;
          document.getElementById('issue-modal-heat').innerHTML = '<span style="' + d.heat_style + '">' + d.heat + '</span>';
          var tl = d.timeline.map(function(t) {
            return '<div style="display:flex; gap:10px; padding:6px 0; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.06); font-size:12px;">' +
              '<div style="color:#5a6e8a; min-width:72px; flex-shrink:0;">' + t[0] + '</div>' +
              '<div style="color:#1b3a6b; line-height:1.4;">' + t[1] + '</div></div>';
          }).join('');
          var critics = d.critics.map(function(c) {
            return '<div style="font-size:12px; color:#5a6e8a; padding:4px 0; line-height:1.4;">· ' + c + '</div>';
          }).join('');
          document.getElementById('issue-modal-body').innerHTML =
            '<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr; border:1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.09); border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; margin-bottom:14px;">' +
              '<div style="padding:12px 14px; border-right:1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.09);">' +
                '<div style="font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\',monospace; font-size:7px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#b8860b; margin-bottom:5px;">' + d.for_label + '</div>' +
                '<div style="font-family:\'Nunito\',sans-serif; font-size:12px; color:#1b3a6b; line-height:1.5;">' + d.for_text + '</div>' +
              '</div>' +
              '<div style="display:flex; align-items:center; padding:0 8px; background:#f8f9fd;">' +
                '<div style="font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\',monospace; font-size:9px; color:#5a6e8a; font-weight:600;">vs</div>' +
              '</div>' +
              '<div style="padding:12px 14px;">' +
                '<div style="font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\',monospace; font-size:7px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#b8860b; margin-bottom:5px;">' + d.against_label + '</div>' +
                '<div style="font-family:\'Nunito\',sans-serif; font-size:12px; color:#1b3a6b; line-height:1.5;">' + d.against_text + '</div>' +
              '</div>' +
            '</div>' +
            '<div style="background:#f8f9fd; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 14px; margin-bottom:12px;">' +
              '<div style="font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\',monospace; font-size:7px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#b8860b; margin-bottom:6px;">' + d.who_label + '</div>' +
              '<div style="font-family:\'Nunito\',sans-serif; font-size:13px; color:#1b3a6b; line-height:1.5;">' + d.position + '</div>' +
            '</div>' +
            '<div style="margin-bottom:12px;">' +
              '<div style="font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\',monospace; font-size:7px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#b8860b; margin-bottom:6px;">What\'s happened</div>' +
              tl +
            '</div>' +
            '<div style="margin-bottom:12px;">' +
              '<div style="font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\',monospace; font-size:7px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#b8860b; margin-bottom:6px;">What critics say</div>' +
              critics +
            '</div>' +
            '<div style="font-size:10px; color:#8a9ab8; padding-top:10px; border-top:1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.09); line-height:1.5;">Sources: ' + d.source + '</div>';
          var overlay = document.getElementById('issue-modal-overlay');
          overlay.style.display = 'flex';
          document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        }

        function issueModalClose() {
          document.getElementById('issue-modal-overlay').style.display = 'none';
          document.body.style.overflow = '';
        }

        document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e) {
          if (e.key === 'Escape') issueModalClose();
        });
      </script>
      <% end %>

      <%# ── SIDEBAR ── %>
      <div class="dp-sidebar">

